5. U-04, IS AN OWNER QUESTION FORCED?
   a mandatory requirement naming a load state for source-only operation: none (section 1)
   the kit's own caps at 9 V: F1 0997010 at its 80 C column 7.3 A (the hottest air 62.1 C): 59.5 W at VBAT; at its 0 C column 9.8 A: 79.8 W; the
     interconnect after D-06 at 20 A: 162.9 W; the entry's limit and H3's line are settings, not capabilities (MAKER, INFERRED)
   REQ-015 states no source current capability: every figure here takes the source as holding its voltage (named)
   against section 3's states at their plan figure: in the hottest air F1's 80 C column caps a 9 V source under PS-TYP 63 W (MAKER, INFERRED);
     the cold states against its 0 C column: none over; a 15 A MINI 58 V (its 80 C column 11 A) would admit 89.6 W, with D-06's band
     re-rated to it: a part choice, not the source's capability (MAKER, INFERRED)
   so NO owner question is forced: no approved requirement names a load REQ-015's 9 V must carry, and where a part caps a named
     state at 9 V another part lifts it, so no arrangement-independent cap exists (INFERRED)

